# Round 14 — deep review of the D44–D49 cascade (2026-10-02)

Scope: the five unpushed commits `7cac12d..4fadfad` (D47 diagnostics,
D48 installer, D49 verify rows, D44-S2 attach mode, plan consolidation).
Method: the deep-pr-review-lean multi-lens pass over a detached worktree
(branch mode, chat-only) — ground truth computed once (2,854-line diff,
32 files, all hand-authored); lenses Correctness/Security/Tests/
Performance/Product-AC/Cleanup/Hazard-grid dispatched as read-only child
agents (roster below; tier-named subagents unavailable in this runtime —
lenses ran at session default, a disclosed cost), verification from
source by the orchestrator. 40 candidate findings, 15 unverified
questions; adjudication kept 33 (7 Blocking, 26 Advisory), merged 7
duplicates, dropped 0 without a named falsifier.

**Verdict: changes-requested — all seven Blocking findings and every
Actionable Advisory fixed in this round's closing commit; two findings
resolved as recorded boundaries with measured justification.**

## Blocking findings (all fixed)

- **B1 — verify's store/lock/port rows read the CLIENT dir while the
  wrapper puts the store at `<dir>/falkordb`** (`--standalone-data-dir
  D/falkordb`): every healthy `--data-dir` session false-RED as "NO live
  supervisor" and the stale-port row could never fire. Fixed:
  `verify_checks::store_artifact_dir` resolves the artifact dir (the
  falkordb layout when its artifacts exist, the bare dir otherwise);
  the lock and port reads ride it. Tests:
  `store_artifact_dir_prefers_the_falkordb_layout`.
- **B2 — `--install-block` destroyed unreadable instruction files**
  (`unwrap_or_default()` swallowed non-UTF-8 read errors, then
  rewrote the file with only the block). Fixed: only NotFound starts
  empty; every other read error refuses. Evidence: the R14 fix comment
  in `main.rs`; the failure mode is data loss, pinned by inspection of
  the two-line change.
- **B3 — the harness row green-lit on two independent file-wide
  substrings** (install dir mentioned for an unrelated tool + the word
  "exocortex" anywhere). Fixed: the dir and an exocortex binary must
  appear on the SAME line. Test: `harness_check_requires_dir_and_binary_on_one_line`.
- **B4 — an unterminated begin marker duplicated the block on run 1**
  (the splice loop broke, the append arm added a fresh block beside the
  orphaned body). Fixed: an unterminated region runs to EOF and is
  replaced. Test: `install_block_replaces_an_unterminated_region`.
- **B5 — the SSE error-body read was size-bounded but TIME-unbounded**
  (a wedged proxy parked the subscriber: no reconnect, no degradation
  cell — strictly worse than pre-D47). Fixed: the read rides
  `timeout(stall_timeout)`, matching the live-body loop beside it.
  Test: `wedged_error_body_still_fails_within_the_stall_timeout`.
- **B6 — attach.json admitted a userinfo bypass and shell injection**
  (`http://127.0.0.1:1@evil.example/` passes the string-prefix loopback
  check and dials evil — confirmed against `http::Uri` authority
  parsing; the unvalidated backend was interpolated unescaped into the
  file the wrapper `source`s). Fixed: the backend is PARSED — plain
  http, no `@` in the authority, literal loopback host, explicit port —
  and the secrets ride the one-impl `signing::decode_hex32` (also
  closing the hand-rolled-hex cleanup finding; hex cannot carry
  shell-significant bytes). Tests:
  `attach_record_round_trips_and_fails_closed_on_malformation` (the
  userinfo shape now asserted refused).
- **B7 — the attached session's WAL slot leaked and stranded writes**
  (cleanup's `rmdir` cannot remove a sled tree — one
  credential-bearing dir per attached session, forever; pending
  offline writes in it were unreachable by any drain). Fixed: cleanup
  `rm -rf`s the runtime dir UNLESS `--tail-audit` still reports
  `[pending]` entries — then the dir is kept and its path printed.

## Advisory findings (fixed in the same commit)

- **S2/U1 — hostile error-body injection**: control characters from a
  backend body rode into operator logs and agent-facing read stamps.
  Fixed at the source: `sync::sanitize_single_line` flattens every
  control char; test `hostile_error_body_is_flattened_to_one_line`.
- **C7/T2 — banner services green-lit the port PING**: `redis_answers`
  now requires a RESP type marker as the first reply byte; test
  `redis_ping_rejects_silent_and_banner_acceptors`.
- **C6 — uppercase-hex divergence** between Rust validators and the
  wrapper's shell class: the wrapper accepts `A-F` now.
- **S3 — attach.json outlived its owner**: the owner removes it on
  exit (any path) via a Drop guard; attachers never touch it.
- **P2 — the attach probe could hang past its own 20s promise**: one
  runtime hoisted above the retry loop, every attempt bounded to 3s;
  `EXOCORTEX_ATTACH_DEADLINE_MS` tunes the deadline.
- **T1 — the D47 production couplings were untested**: the cell
  record/clear is now driven through the REAL subscriber loop
  (`subscriber_records_and_clears_the_degradation_cell`).
- **T3 — verify's exit code was pinned only from the red side**:
  every verify_rows leg asserts exit == red-row count.
- **T4 — "healthy reads stay registry-identical" proved key-absence**:
  now byte-compares a cell-carrying server against a cell-free one on
  all three reads.
- **T5/A3 — the logging canary self-selected its surface and its name
  overclaimed**: scans `src/main.rs` AND `src/bin/*.rs`, fails any
  tracing-emitting binary without the WARN builder, renamed to what it
  checks.
- **T6 — the live attach suite ran in NO gate**: `verify-release.sh`
  now runs it whenever the bundled runtime resolves (loud skip
  otherwise, the storage-conformance pattern).
- **T7 — the wrapper's attach fail-closed branches were untested**:
  `attach_runtime_failures_refuse_before_the_client_spawns` (three
  shapes; the first draft of this test passed for the WRONG reason —
  quote-broken stubs left the runtime file empty and the wrapper timed
  out instead of refusing — caught and fixed with a heredoc stub).
- **T8 — `backend_status` was listed but never dispatched in test**:
  `stdio_smoke::backend_status_is_dispatchable_over_stdio`.
- **T9 — the attach-record fixture used identical secrets**: distinct
  values, full-struct read-back, per-field env lines, and the userinfo
  refusal leg.
- **T10 — nothing pinned the block's marker self-reference
  invariant**: `block_body_never_contains_its_own_markers`.
- **T11 — wal_roundtrip stamped empty org/user**: distinct values.
- **Cl1/Cl3/Cl5/Cl6/Cl7/Cl8** — dead statement, the FALSE "attach
  consumes the port file" comment (attach consumes attach.json; the
  comment, the RED message, and SKILL.md now tell the truth), the
  pasted read-stamp dance (one `stamped_read` + one `sync_health_json`
  builder), unwarranted `pub` narrowed, the live test now calls the
  lib's own `store_ports_on_dir`, and `StreamErrorCell` aliases the
  config field where it is declared.
- **P3/P4/P5** — verify decodes the WAL once (`pending_and_partitions`),
  harness-config reads are bounded (8 MiB, unreadable → RED), and the
  marker splice keeps a cursor (k regions, one pass).
- **A2 — `attach_to_live_node` had no ungated test**:
  `attach_tests::attach_publishes_owner_env_and_refuses_mismatched_owners`
  boots an in-process owner node, asserts the published env verbatim,
  and asserts a fingerprint-mismatched owner is refused without
  publishing.

## Resolved as recorded boundaries

- **F2 (crash-path credential retention in the mktemp runtime.env)**:
  the proposed startup sweep measured **33s** on this machine (a
  TMPDIR-wide `find`, zero CPU — pure scan latency) — a cost every
  session would pay against a crash-only leak already protected by
  0600-in-0700 and reboot reclamation. Reverted; revisit only with a
  bounded reaper. The finding's other half (slot leak) IS fixed (B7).
- **C8 (conf-file foreign stores and title-rewritten pre-S1 orphans are
  invisible to the ps scan)**: with B1's path fix, the lock-holder +
  recorded-port evidence covers the supervised case; the
  conf-file-launched foreign writer remains beyond a client-side
  check's reach — the verify row text states what it counts.

## Unverified questions — dispositions

- userinfo bypass: CONFIRMED against `http::Uri` parsing and fixed (B6).
- tonic connect/request timeouts: none by default — the P2 fix does not
  rely on them.
- mktemp dir mode: 0700 on macOS/GNU — established, leans on F2's
  boundary note.
- `~/.claude.json` size: mooted by the bounded read (P4).
- RUST_LOG override precedence: the documented
  `with_default_directive`/`from_env_lossy` builder idiom; the canary
  was renamed to claim only what it checks (A3).
- slow-owner attach past 20s: the deadline is now tunable and the
  boundary recorded; D45's real-data run will observe boot times.

