## Final pass addendum (2026-10-02, the fix loop's --final second opinion)

An independent adversarial pass over the post-fix tree (never shown the
round's findings) returned 11 candidates; adjudication kept 9, dropped
1 with a named check, and confirmed the loop was NOT converged:

- **SO-1 (Blocking) — the S3 fix broke attach entirely**: the
  `RemoveAttachOnExit` guard was scoped inside the publish `if let`,
  dropping at the closing brace and deleting `attach.json` at owner
  STARTUP — concurrent sessions could never attach. Fixed: the guard
  lives at serve-loop scope. The ungated tests missed it (they write
  their own records) and the live suite had not run post-fix — the
  final pass is what caught it. Re-verified green live.
- **SO-2 (Blocking) — the B7 keep-guard was inert**: `>/dev/null` sat
  BEFORE the pipe, so grep always read EOF and `rm -rf` always ran —
  pending writes were still deletable. Fixed: stderr-only redirect,
  10k-entry window.
- **SO-3 (Blocking) — the B6 injection surface was half-closed**: a
  quote-bearing URI PATH passes the parsed host checks into the sourced
  env file. Fixed: the record's backend must carry no path and no query.
- **SO-4 (Blocking per the closure rule) — the T4 remedy was recorded
  but never landed** (a batched edit aborted before writing it): the
  byte-identity test now actually exists.
- **SO-8/SO-9/SO-10/SO-11 (Advisory) — fixed**: the wrapper readiness
  window now covers the attach deadline (25s), the owner-path SSE-key
  check accepts uppercase hex like every other validator,
  `--install-block` writes atomically (mode-preserving temp+rename),
  and an empty `HOME` no longer probes CWD-relative harness configs.
- **UQ4 → fixed**: the attach record carries the owner's `org` and the
  attacher refuses a different `--org` (the cross-org variant of the
  empty-graph-next-door hazard).
- **SO-5 dropped** — `cargo fmt --all -- --check` exits 0 on the exact
  tree; the quoted worker indentation is rustfmt-legal.
- **SO-6/SO-7 (docs) — fixed**: the plan rows' stale citations (the
  pre-rename canary name, the false port-file rationale, pids→ports).
- **Boundaries recorded**: the owner-death-vs-attacher race (UQ3 — a
  session attached moments before the owner dies serves a frozen
  snapshot until its own reconnect; D47 surfaces the degradation);
  the attacher-vs-wrapper deadline interplay is now aligned (25s > 20s).

cost: 1 agent (complex) · second opinion ran (--final) · pass_type full
